From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:32:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: route the verified helper's large reservations into
 the Social Club layout

PLA-476, active only with PLAYPORT_SC_LAYOUT=1 and a complete boot layout.
SocialClubHelper.exe's chrome_elf/libcef PartitionAlloc pools, their
metadata regions, Oilpan's cage and V8's 8 GB sandbox step get fixed real
slots and report what was asked. Every other giant reserve from the helper
fails with STATUS_NO_MEMORY instead of reaching the soft-pool grant
(PLA-477). Commits, protects and frees inside a slot's real range are
allowed only for its owner; a grant is released as a whole by its owner or
at its owner's exit through the existing process teardown, and the slot is
held again. Reported tails beyond the real ranges are logged, not enforced.
The helper is told a 2 TB HighestUserAddress so V8 takes its partial
sandbox (report only). One helper owns the slots at a time.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-29-sc-stock-cef-probe.md
Offered-upstream: no
